  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Open since 1953 and run by three generations, Astoux et Brun is a Cannes seafood institution, right at the foot of Le Suquet. Seafood platters (Boutrais oysters, Gillardeau oysters), mussels marinière, fish soup, sole meunière, lemon tart: a lively, no-frills brasserie atmosphere.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to a directory specialising in dog-friendly restaurants (rated 4/5), the establishment welcomes dogs. The restaurant's official website does not explicitly mention a dog policy: it's best to ask on arrival, especially since the house doesn't take reservations and you may have to wait for a table, particularly on the terrace. Correction on the hours: service runs in two shifts, 12pm-2pm and 7pm-11:30pm, every day — not continuously from 11am to 11pm as previously stated.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: no reservations here — arrive before 12:30pm or after 9pm to limit the wait, especially on the terrace with your dog.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>You're just steps from Le Suquet and the harbour of Cannes: a good chance to end your walk with your dog through the lanes of the old quarter after the meal.</p>
    </div>

